;">THE MICROMANAGER FINAL BOSS</h2></div></td></tr>
<tr><td align=3D"left" class=3D"text" style=3D"background:#FFFFFF;font-size=
:0px;padding:0 16px;word-break:break-word;"><div style=3D"font-family:Georg=
ia, serif;font-size:16px;font-weight:400;line-height:22px;text-align:left;c=
olor:#121212;">
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">The use of psychological stratagems and pi=
tchside or locker-room sabotage has long been employed by football managers=
 trying to give their teams an edge over visiting rivals. Whether it=E2=80=
=99s placing the pegs too high or the seats too low, painting the walls an =
aggression-lowering shade of pink or deliberately moving the advertising ho=
ardings to prevent long throws, there are apparently no stones conniving co=
aching staff will leave unturned if they think their team=E2=80=99s chances=
 of winning may be improved by such shenanigans. Almost 40 years ago, Wimbl=
edon=E2=80=99s Crazy Gang famously used to leave visitors to Plough Lane wi=
thout any hot water, a plan that seemed stunning in its simplicity, until y=
ou realise =E2=80=93 as Football Daily has just done after nearly 40 years =
=E2=80=93 that footballers generally tend not to shower until <em>after</em=
> the game is over, rendering their attempt at disruption decidedly redunda=
nt.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">A man who has previously attracted ridicul=
e for <a href=3D"https://ablink.editorial.theguardian.com/ss/c/u001.Yw_JkLM=
EmFuifc_XG18IRyTNtZQ7fIEMgszcCSneHEDPz9cP19ucotlc3OZlAKOo6ezrS79vkYkpwfVWHr=
6TR2PtpHCfPStt01ZiyrqWtUvpFtdRg8x9YFZSZRd_Uohq3NU13faZB1mZOdSFy6KrEz5ApyMhq=
Twd2T0bYGrLttba5GZZjmwW4D9pKtOMpE-qjMRtOGYqpm4_0oMyyIi9pGOma8i6aSoY5puJEmAw=
0lRF-BCy-XG43fRiOW62Gr_DUfEMeoBlsZjq9YKP2wKz6huW9HC-5y2QkgGYNMw33KRSQ0lhMEY=
LTath9gXt3A8GDOEUseSbw5yJ-XOZnPs3KQ/4ty/rpY0T_MMQhySnHAVnoWczg/h29/h001.pu1=
JOVIU6CqX2Zg53Fm_B7ANmHOsOTWYJ9iPhH0atw8" style=3D"color: #0077B6;">hiring =
a team of pickpockets</a> to pinch his players=E2=80=99 watches, phones and=
 wallets during a team dinner to teach them the value of vigilance and focu=
s, it ought to come as no surprise that Mikel Arteta has now hit upon the p=
sychological wheeze <a href=3D"https://ablink.editorial.theguardian.com/ss/=
c/u001.Yw_JkLMEmFuifc_XG18IRyTNtZQ7fIEMgszcCSneHEBgtjhYSJYcaNsDra0BxnPgCG7H=
Uaxu3cpi5DAF4Qr0-BQXRg1ZC-e9heps4L84vJKq3r_Od4AwlKIywftrjyF3Fri1Fx50HLKrWnw=
dsBEDLshBz7LEMNxDp2fTYQBqNmWK-Gb65WEUk3M7SSbPulRaOkPhN2s2tOr-Kwtz2Ih0GdmXd5=
pXif5kAOs6VUiAPajCE6HLB40W72dsxpSld-pX7CxjVjMY6eiPf0lz0eanKqStpwYA5h02oKceO=
Fpylso4t_82MX_zab9OwCMek2eR/4ty/rpY0T_MMQhySnHAVnoWczg/h30/h001.Qc_t1KiaiYj=
Im5YXuoXIDrJ3q8pQ84x6PcpLFjOLVEE" style=3D"color: #0077B6;">of disrupting h=
is own team=E2=80=99s preparations</a> for matches as a way of keeping them=
 on their toes. The Arsenal manager has revealed that he occasionally has d=
ressing-room thermostats turned up to 11, delays meal and transport times, =
or has physio room massage beds =E2=80=9Cdisappeared=E2=80=9D to ensure Ars=
enal=E2=80=99s finest are prepared for any curveballs life might pitch thei=
r way. And while such half-baked amateur psychology will almost certainly p=
rovide more grist to the mill of Arteta haterz, if inducing mild anxiety in=
 Declan Rice and Bukayo Saka over a toasty canteen or slightly late bus is =
all it takes to finally win a league title, then who are we to carp?</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">=E2=80=9CI love those challenges,=E2=80=9D=
 parped Arteta. =E2=80=9CI try to create them in pre-season. So when they h=
appen, we already experience them and we already know. So, get to the stadi=
um very late, change the routine as soon as the players have to do somethin=
g else. Because when it happens, and it can happen, you can miss the flight=
, the train can be delayed, there=E2=80=99s so much traffic, and I don=E2=
=80=99t want the players, the staff as well, panicking.=E2=80=9D Of course,=
 our more astute reader will have already clocked that Arsenal=E2=80=99s fl=
ight to Naples this week was delayed by several hours, prompting the cancel=
lation of their pre-match press duties.</p>
<p style=3D"margin: 0 0 16px 0;">While Arsenal=E2=80=99s was only one of se=
veral hundred flights from UK airports disrupted or cancelled due to <a hre=
f=3D"https://ablink.editorial.theguardian.com/ss/c/u001.Yw_JkLMEmFuifc_XG18=
IRyTNtZQ7fIEMgszcCSneHEAsxWg7d8sWyUjf1CJIvNP3Ra6GvjYb1Fjw8Aht3c0zBYDCGIQara=
O19Qb4rvxHtsj6BJ2PxlaCC7CAK7UztR7kfhXVP7OtaJPGNuVPYjmBFktSn5zvp7AQQCJlW15AV=
5vAYHAT3gkVyNoMgZG9ECBsdNWzEQnzOXcgyYESQwpjWDtumuNwHe7XgKNIcydRFFHx4aZ1aT5E=
VQyMsbWrDOZTYi_ChGjI6LZ-n3QI1o4Efimy5w8sMH1FknSmlfwdFV4LlSsr-Z7Iq-B5-JmVkqA=
7lVqiLyUzaS_Q9fJWhgmZjo0vdBvO-GYwAjHLvJ3d85I/4ty/rpY0T_MMQhySnHAVnoWczg/h31=
/h001.5zuaXLubaoGOAOlpNFbDPMsEZWCLvbUcyJlZrwbR7bA" style=3D"color: #0077B6;=
">an air traffic control =E2=80=9Cglitch=E2=80=9D</a>, it behoves Football =
Daily to point out there is no suggestion that a slightly weird 44-year-old=
 from San Sebasti=C3=A1n was responsible for you and your pals missing out =
on that eagerly anticipated lads=E2=80=99 trip to Benidorm. We also know th=
at while stressed-out passengers in overcrowded departure lounges across th=
e UK were effing, jeffing and generally losing their minds, the footballers=
 of Arsenal were =E2=80=93 due in no small part to Arteta=E2=80=99s mind ga=
mes =E2=80=93 presumably waiting in the business lounge to board their well=
-appointed jet in a state of carefully orchestrated zen.</p>
